        "C": "2",
        "D": "3",
        "E": "4"
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "explanation": "Quadrilateral → 4 vertices. Diagonals = n(n−3)/2 = 4*1/2=2.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Use diagonals formula.",
        "2. Compute 4×1/2=2."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Quad → always 2 diagonals."
    },

    {
